From c0b2d599a4e8d972f5ae34def63d18254599ef66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:48:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a chat mid-turn defers the unloaded-chat notice
 instead of crashing the sweep; HX014 flags swallowed contextmanager yields
 [daveey]

find_session_db caught the caller's own error at its yield (a chat mid-turn refusing the
notice row: "Session has an active turn lease"), yielded again and Python raised
"generator didn't stop after throw()". The sweeper logged that with a traceback every
30 s until the turn ended (hub 10-27: 277x over 2h20m; kanban-e5babca565).

- find_session_db opens/locates the store inside the try, yields outside any handler
  (ExitStack keeps the store open across the yield): caller errors propagate as themselves.
- _persist_notice: SessionTurnLeaseLostError = busy -> rewind, one INFO "deferred: chat
  busy", retried next pass (passive and wake-worker paths). Other failures unchanged.
- Overdue guard: a notice whose claim was rewound and is still waiting >15 min logs ONE
  WARNING per board/card/chat with the reason.
- scripts/code_health HX014: a @contextmanager whose broad except around a yield doesn't
  re-raise and can yield again. 0 hits on main after this fix; one-shot suppress-and-log
  helpers are not flagged.

Tests: tests/tui_gateway/test_kanban_unloaded_busy.py (real opener + real turn lease; red
3/4 on base), tests/scripts/test_code_health_contextmanager_rule.py.
